[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 1"""
 date="2026-11-23T13:31:14Z"
 content="""
Demand loading Annex state would also allow freeing Annex state when a
repository has not been accessed in a long time. As p2phttp scales to large
numbers of repositories, the memory used for Annex states for each repository
(times the number of jobs) might eventually become a scalability problem,
so it would be good to have an architecture that allows freeing unused
states.

And git-annex got a shiny new LRU cache implementation recently, 
that could be used for this.
"""]]
